{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he did not set his heart to this either.</b> To grasp the distinction that applied also in this plague between the divine agency and the agency of the sorcerers: the act of Elohim, blessed be He, was an alteration in the nature of the river — which is entirely incorruptible — transforming it into true blood, so that the fish in it died; whereas the act of the magicians was an alteration in something already corruptible, or perhaps mere optical illusion."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:46.215093906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}